# Rationale for disabled checks (see ADR 0006):
#
# -performance-enum-size: LogLevel/LogFormat in src/common/config.h
#     are not on any hot path; narrowing the underlying type to save
#     3 bytes is a micro-optimization that obscures intent. Applied
#     repo-wide because the same cost/benefit holds for any future
#     small-cardinality config enum.
#
# -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage: LOG_TRACE/DEBUG/INFO/WARN/ERROR/
#     CRITICAL in src/common/log.h are thin wrappers over spdlog
#     SPDLOG_* macros, which capture __FILE__/__LINE__/__func__ at
#     the call site. The spdlog logging API is macro-based by
#     design; rewriting the facade around std::source_location to
#     satisfy the linter is not justified scope for Phase 0 and may
#     be revisited when IPC logging lands in Phase 1.
#
# Both were originally observed only under the older docker clang-tidy
# (18.1.3) and not on the host. ADR 0043 moved the docker image onto the
# same clang-tidy 20.1.2 as the host (native Ubuntu noble-updates
# clang-20), so the canonical CI and the host now run the identical
# linter with no version drift. The two checks stay disabled on their
# own merits (above), not because of any host/docker divergence. See
# docs/DECISIONS/0043-toolchain-source-native-clang20-supersede-0006.md.
#
# HeaderFilterRegex limits analysis to our own headers. Third-party
# dependencies are pulled in via FetchContent with the SYSTEM keyword
# (see CMakeLists.txt), so their headers reach the compiler as -isystem
# includes; clang-tidy skips system headers by default, so the substring
# include pattern above no longer matches build/_deps/*/include/
# (tl::expected, googletest, protobuf) and no explicit exclude is needed.
# (The exclude was also unparseable by the old docker clang-tidy 18.1.3,
# which did not know the ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex key; since ADR 0043 the
# docker linter is clang-tidy 20, but SYSTEM makes the exclude unnecessary
# regardless, so it stays out.)
---
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '(src|include)/.*'
